  "raw_text": "Step 1: Identify the structure of the magic square and the given values.\nStep 2: Recognize that the sum of each row, column, and diagonal must be the same. Let this common sum be \\(S\\).\nStep 3: Write equations for the sums of the rows, columns, and diagonals using the given values and the variable \\(n\\).\n\nFor the first row: \\((n-3) + 3 + (n+1) = S\\)\nSimplifying: \\(2n + 1 = S\\)\n\nFor the second row: \\((n+2) + (2n-9) + 1 = S\\)\nSimplifying: \\(3n - 6 = S\\)\n\nFor the third row: \\(2 + n + (n-1) = S\\)\nSimplifying: \\(2n + 1 = S\\)\n\nFor the first column: \\((n-3) + (n+2) + 2 = S\\)\nSimplifying: \\(2n + 1 = S\\)\n\nFor the second column: \\(3 + (2n-9) + n = S\\)\nSimplifying: \\(3n - 6 = S\\)\n\nFor the third column: \\((n+1) + 1 + (n-1) = S\\)\nSimplifying: \\(2n + 1 = S\\)\n\nFor the main diagonal from top left to bottom right: \\((n-3) + (2n-9) + (n-1) = S\\)\nSimplifying: \\(4n - 13 = S\\)\n\nFor the other main diagonal: \\((n+1) + (2n-9) + 2 = S\\)\nSimplifying: \\(3n - 6 = S\\)\n\nStep 4: Since all these expressions equal \\(S\\), we can set any two of them equal to each other to solve for \\(n\\). Using \\(2n + 1 = 3n - 6\\):\n\\[2n + 1 = 3n - 6\\]\nSubtract \\(2n\\) from both sides:\n\\[1 = n - 6\\]\nAdd 6 to both sides:\n\\[n = 7\\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{7}<|im_end|>",
  "reforward_peak_bytes": 15556848640,
